## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect end-to-end edge ML workflows on GCP with enterprise-grade privacy, governance, and operational considerations beyond model accuracy.

## Key Concepts
- Edge model distillation and Vertex AI training pipelines
- Edge artifact distribution via Pub/Sub and Cloud CDN
- Regional canary deployments and per-tenant quotas
- Data residency, CMEK, and DLP for privacy compliance
- On-device telemetry, drift monitoring, and automated rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example config for edge rollout policy
const rollout = {
  region: 'us-east1',
  quota: 1000,
  canary: {
    percentage: 10,
    duration: '2h'
  },
  validation: {
    latencyTarget: '<100ms',
    driftThreshold: 0.05,
    minSampleSize: 1000
  },
  rollback: {
    auto: true,
    cooldown: '30min'
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?
